## 2.1.x.x System Configuration Overview Screen

### a. UI Specifications

#### System Configuration Overview Screen

**Brief Description**
This screen displays all configurable system parameter groups in card format. It allows the authorized actor to review and update system configuration settings for credit policy, production capacity, working shift, delivery rule, waste rule, and priority rule. When the actor selects a configuration card, the system opens a pop-up containing the current values of that configuration group, where the actor can view and edit the settings in the same interface.

**Mockup Screen(s)**

* Main screen: **System Configuration Overview Screen**
* Pop-up screens:

  * **Credit Policy Pop-up**
  * **Production Capacity Pop-up**
  * **Working Shift Pop-up**
  * **Delivery Rule Pop-up**
  * **Waste Rule Pop-up**
  * **Priority Rule Pop-up**

**UI Description / Requirements / Notes**

---

### 1. Main Area

#### 1.1 Screen Title

* Field Name: Screen Title
* Type: Label
* Value: `System Configuration`
* Description: Displays the name of the current screen.

#### 1.2 Screen Introduction

* Field Name: Screen Introduction
* Type: Text
* Description: Briefly explains that this screen is used to manage configurable system rules and operational parameters.

---

### 2. Configuration Card Section

This section displays configuration categories as clickable cards.

#### 2.1 Credit Policy Card

* Field Name: Credit Policy Card
* Type: Action Card
* Description: Displays summary information of credit-related settings such as customer debt limit, overdue threshold, or approval condition.
* Action:

  * Click → open **Credit Policy Pop-up**

#### 2.2 Production Capacity Card

* Field Name: Production Capacity Card
* Type: Action Card
* Description: Displays summary information of production lead time, daily capacity, or related production planning parameters.
* Action:

  * Click → open **Production Capacity Pop-up**

#### 2.3 Working Shift Card

* Field Name: Working Shift Card
* Type: Action Card
* Description: Displays summary information of configured working time, number of shifts, or working days.
* Action:

  * Click → open **Working Shift Pop-up**

#### 2.4 Delivery Rule Card

* Field Name: Delivery Rule Card
* Type: Action Card
* Description: Displays summary information of delivery buffer rule or shipping preparation rule.
* Action:

  * Click → open **Delivery Rule Pop-up**

#### 2.5 Waste Rule Card

* Field Name: Waste Rule Card
* Type: Action Card
* Description: Displays summary information of waste percentage or material allowance rule.
* Action:

  * Click → open **Waste Rule Pop-up**

#### 2.6 Priority Rule Card

* Field Name: Priority Rule Card
* Type: Action Card
* Description: Displays summary information of priority criteria used for order or production scheduling.
* Action:

  * Click → open **Priority Rule Pop-up**

---

### 3. Common Card Information

Each card should contain:

* Configuration name
* Short description
* Current summary value(s)
* Last updated date/time
* Last updated by
* Visual icon for quick recognition

**UI Notes**

* Actor does not edit data directly on the overview screen.
* Edit action is performed only inside the related pop-up.
* Each card should be visually separated and easy to identify.
* Card layout should support responsive grid view.

---

### 4. Common Pop-up Structure

When the actor clicks a card, the system displays a pop-up for that configuration type.

Each pop-up should include:

#### 4.1 Pop-up Title

* Shows the configuration group name, for example:

  * `Credit Policy`
  * `Production Capacity`
  * `Working Shift`

#### 4.2 Configuration Fields

* Displays the current values of the selected configuration group.
* Fields are editable in the same pop-up.

#### 4.3 Save Button

* Label: `Save`
* Action: Saves updated configuration values.

#### 4.4 Cancel Button

* Label: `Cancel`
* Action: Closes the pop-up without saving changes.

#### 4.5 Close Icon

* Action: Closes the pop-up.

**UI Notes**

* View and edit are combined in one pop-up.
* Existing values must be preloaded when the pop-up is opened.
* Validation must be performed before saving.
* The pop-up should block background interaction until closed.

---

### 5. Example Fields by Pop-up Type

#### 5.1 Credit Policy Pop-up

Possible fields:

* Maximum Debt Limit
* Overdue Days Threshold
* Credit Approval Required Condition
* Note

#### 5.2 Production Capacity Pop-up

Possible fields:

* Standard Production Lead Time
* Daily Production Capacity
* Overtime Capacity Allowance
* Note

#### 5.3 Working Shift Pop-up

Possible fields:

* Number of Shifts per Day
* Shift Start Time
* Shift End Time
* Working Days
* Note

#### 5.4 Delivery Rule Pop-up

Possible fields:

* Delivery Buffer Days
* Default Delivery Preparation Time
* Note

#### 5.5 Waste Rule Pop-up

Possible fields:

* Waste Percentage
* Material Allowance Rule
* Note

#### 5.6 Priority Rule Pop-up

Possible fields:

* Priority Criteria
* Priority Score / Weight
* Urgent Order Rule
* Note

---

### 6. Message

Suggested system messages:

* Save success: with `"Configuration updated successfully."`
* Validation error: with `"Please enter valid configuration values."`
* No permission: with `"You do not have permission to update this configuration."`
* Unsaved changes warning: with `"Unsaved changes will be lost. Do you want to continue?"`

